identity":true,"weighted_defect_sum16":true},"class_signature":{"edge_axis_reflection":[1,1],"half_turn":[2],"identity":[0],"quarter_turn":[3,3],"vertex_axis_reflection":[3,3]},"defect_definition":"delta(g)=dim(V+gV)-dim(V)=7-dim(V intersect gV)","defect_histogram":{"0":1,"1":2,"2":1,"3":4},"defect_sum":16,"relation_space":{"ambient_dimension":20,"dimension":7,"field_labels":[2,3,6,4],"prime_labels":[2,3,5,7,13]},"schema":"w33.pass652.d8_descent_defect_signature.v1","status":"PASS","theorem":"The obstruction to forgetting the ordered conductor frame has an exact D8 class signature. The descent defect delta(g)=dim(V+gV)-7 takes values 0,1,2,3 with multiplicities 1,2,1,4. The two edge-axis reflections have defect one, the half-turn has defect two, and the quarter-turns plus vertex-axis reflections have defect three. These ranks agree over Q and modulo 2,3,5,7,11,13, so the obstruction is integral rather than a modular accident. In particular the full relation-space stabilizer inside D8 is trivial."}
